CheeseCutter 2.11R — Hypercut

Hypercut is a major desktop editing, arrangement, audio, Help and export update.

Hypercut enhancements by arch0N.

The embedded C64 music driver remains unchanged.

TRACK OVERVIEW

- From top to bottom, the Track Overview contains the grey Timeline bar,
  Voice 1 lane, Voice 2 lane and Voice 3 lane.

Timeline

- The grey top bar is an interactive song Timeline.
- Click to place the global song position; click and drag to scrub across the
  complete song.
- During playback, scrubbing restarts playback from that position.
- Double-click to set the active voice's F1 play-from marker.
- Per-voice arrows show all three F1 play-from positions.
- Speed dots show voice speed events, and the Timeline follows playback
  automatically.
- Use the scrollbar, mouse wheel or trackpad to explore long songs.

Voice lanes

- Each voice lane contains a narrow upper LOOP strip and Sequence blocks below.
- The LOOP strip shows the voice's LOOP start position.
- Click above a Sequence block to set it as that voice's independent LOOP
  target.
- The lower lane contains distinct, auto-generated, colour-coded Sequence
  blocks; repeated uses of the same Sequence number retain the same colour.
- Note previews reveal the musical content of each block.
- Click a block to select it and jump to its editor position.
- Shift-click selects a range within one voice lane.
- Drag to move a block or selected range.
- Option-drag on macOS or Alt-drag on Windows duplicates a block or range.
- Copy, Paste and Delete shortcuts edit blocks.
- The plus control creates and inserts the next unused Sequence.
- Return or Tab opens a single selected block directly in F6.
- Only one active block or range is selected at a time, and selections and
  movement remain confined to their voice lane.

F6 PATTERN EDITOR

- Select complete rows with the mouse or keyboard, then copy, paste or delete
  the selected range.
- Slow drag-selection auto-scrolls near the upper and lower edges.
- Row-number colours relate subtly to their Track Overview block.
- Adjustable beat-row highlighting is saved with the tune.
- Return follows referenced Pulse, Filter, Chord or Command data; returning
  from a table restores the original F6 position.
- Keypad 0 auditions the current row once for all voices and steps down.
- Keyboard note audition is more reliable, including short taps.

INSTRUMENTS

- Copy and paste complete Instruments.
- Select, copy and paste individual Instrument bytes.
- Instrument pointer fields open their Wave, Pulse or Filter start row.
- Returning from a program table restores the Instrument editor position.
- Selecting an Instrument synchronises all three program-table previews.
- Byte- and nibble-aware Quick Help explains the current Instrument field.

WAVE, PULSE AND FILTER TABLES

- Select complete row ranges with the mouse or keyboard, then copy, paste or
  delete the selected rows.
- Slow drag-selection auto-scrolls near table edges.
- Clipboard data remains restricted to its originating table type.
- Instrument pointer changes immediately update the related table preview.
- Expanded byte-, nibble- and value-aware Quick Help explains table commands.

FILES AND EXPORT

- A full mouse-driven file browser provides filtering.
- Directory and filename fields support direct keyboard and mouse focus.
- In the Instrument editor, Load and Save icons affect the current Instrument;
  elsewhere, they affect the Song.
- Save Songs as .ct directly from the GUI.
- Export .sid and .prg files directly from the Save dialogue.
- Load and save individual .cti Instruments.
- Normal SID and PRG export no longer requires leaving the application.

AUDIO AND PLAYBACK

- The three-voice oscilloscope provides clickable mute controls.
- Control+1, Control+2 and Control+3 share the same mute state as the
  oscilloscope.
- Voice mute settings survive stop, restart and every playback route.
- The default audio request is 48000 Hz with a 128-sample buffer.
- Runtime sample-rate and buffer selection is available, down to 32 samples
  where supported.
- Runtime PAL/NTSC session playback switching does not change exported song
  timing.
- Runtime audio interpolation control is available.
- SDL2 audio-device compatibility and playback stability are improved.

SUBTUNES

- Select and edit subtunes directly from the main interface.

INTERFACE

- Click fields, tables and pattern data to focus and position the cursor.
- Four colour themes are included: CheeseCutter Classic, C64, C64 Midnight and
  Hypercut Neon.
- Bottom controls provide Fullscreen, theme selection, Load, Save, Keyjam,
  Audio Settings and contextual Help.

HELP AND QUICK HELP

- Contextual Quick Help has been rewritten as a three-line display.
- Byte-, nibble-, value- and row-aware information appears while editing.
- Chord shuffle Help follows the real shuffle region at speed $00 or $01.
- F12 opens detailed Help for the current editor context.
- F12 Help provides clickable topics, mouse-wheel scrolling and pinned topic
  headings.
- Each Help topic remembers its own scroll position.
- Detailed Instrument, Wave, Pulse, Filter, Chord and Sequence references are
  included.
- Shortcut labels come from canonical keyboard bindings.
- Command, Control, Option and Alt names match the current platform.

PLATFORMS

- macOS arm64 application release.
- Native Windows x64 support.
- Platform-specific desktop application icons.
